From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: wake DPMS when the consumer reconnects

PowerDevil's idle timeout (or any "turn off screen") puts the workspace into DPMS TurningOff and the
kscreen effect fades the whole scene to transparent. On Android the panel's power belongs to Android,
so this output never reports DpmsMode::Off and nothing ends the fade except input -- and on touch,
DpmsInputEventFilter wants a double tap. The user reopens PowOS and sees only the Android wallpaper.

A consumer reconnect is the app coming to the front, i.e. the screen is on and showing us: request
DPMS On there.
---
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp	2026-10-17 02:34:03
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp	2026-10-17 02:34:18
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "wayland/textinput_v2.h"
 #include "wayland/textinput_v3.h"
 #include "wayland_server.h"
+#include "workspace.h"
 
 #include <QFutureWatcher>
 #include <QScopeGuard>
@@ -544,6 +545,15 @@
     qCDebug(KWIN_ANLAND) << "reconnect: camera request result" << cameraRequestResult;
     if (m_inFallback) {
         return;
+    }
+    // PowOS: a consumer reconnect means the user just brought the app to the front -- the Android
+    // screen is on and showing us. A DPMS-off requested while they were away (PowerDevil's idle
+    // timeout, a "turn off screen" action) leaves the scene faded out by the kscreen effect, and
+    // nothing else ends it: this output can't switch Android's panel, so it never reports
+    // DpmsMode::Off, and DpmsInputEventFilter wants a double tap on touch. Turn it back on here.
+    if (workspace() && workspace()->dpmsState() != Workspace::DpmsState::On) {
+        qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "reconnect: waking from DPMS off";
+        workspace()->requestDpmsState(Workspace::DpmsState::On);
     }
     m_outputs[0]->resumeRendering();
     qCDebug(KWIN_ANLAND) << "reconnect: render loop resumed";
